## MANDATORY FEATURE SCAFFOLD (DO NOT DEVIATE)

When adding a new domain resource (e.g. Events), **mirror Users / Roles**. Do not invent alternate folder layouts, controllers without `BaseController`, ad-hoc fetchers, or untyped API calls.

### Gold-standard references
- **CRUD list resource:** Users (`UserController`, `routes/api/v1/users.php`, `pages/user/*`, `services/user.ts`, `types/user.ts`)
- **Settings CRUD resource:** Roles (`RoleController`, `pages/settings/roles/*`, `services/role.ts`, `types/role.ts`) **and** Packages (`PackageController`, `pages/settings/packages/*`, `services/package.ts`, `types/package.ts`)

### A) Backend checklist (every new resource)

1. **Migration** — `database/migrations/..._create_<table>_table.php` (+ alter migrations as needed)
2. **Model** — `app/Models/<Name>.php`
   - `$fillable`, casts, relations
   - Use `SoftDeletes` when trash/restore is required (Users/Roles do)
3. **Enum(s)** (if needed) — `app/Enums/`
4. **Controller** — `app/Http/Controllers/Api/<Name>Controller.php`
   - **MUST** `extends BaseController`
   - Set protected props only where possible:
     - `$model`
     - `$searchableFields`
     - `$sortableFields`
     - `$relationships`
     - `$validationRules` (`store` / `update`)
   - Override `store`/`update`/etc. **only** for domain-specific logic (password hash, role sync, file upload) — still use `$this->successResponse` / `$this->createdResponse` / `$this->notFoundResponse` from traits
   - Inherited from `BaseController`: `index`, `search`, `store`, `show`, `update`, `destroy`, `trashed`, `restore`, `forceDestroy`, `bulkDelete`, `bulkRestore`, `bulkForceDelete`, activity logging
5. **API v1 route file** — `routes/api/v1/<resource>.php`
   - Wrap in `Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')`
   - Permission middleware per action (`permission:view …`, `create`, `edit`, `delete`)
   - Standard shape (see Users):
     - `GET /` index, `POST /` store, `GET /{id}` show, `PATCH /{id}` update, `DELETE /{id}` destroy
     - Bulk: `DELETE /bulk/delete`, `POST /bulk/restore`, `DELETE /bulk/force-delete`
     - Soft delete: `GET /trashed/list`, `POST /{id}/restore`, `DELETE /{id}/force`
6. **Register routes** — in `routes/api.php` under `Route::prefix('v1')`:
   ```php
   Route::prefix('<resource>')->group(base_path('routes/api/v1/<resource>.php'));
   ```
7. **Permissions** — add to `database/seeders/RolePermissionSeeder.php` (and reseed / sync as needed)
8. **Do not** put resource routes only in `web.php`; API belongs under `/api/v1`.

### B) Frontend checklist (every new list/CRUD resource)

1. **Types** — `resources/js/src/types/<name>.ts`
   - Prefer extending `ITimestamped` from `types/common.ts`
   - Export from `resources/js/src/types/index.ts`
2. **Service** — `resources/js/src/services/<name>.ts`
   - **MUST** `extends BaseApi<T>` from `services/baseApi.ts`
   - Constructor: `super("/<resource>")` matching API prefix
   - Export singleton: `export const <name>Api = new <Name>Api()`
   - Add extra methods only when needed (like Organization profile/logo)
3. **Page folder** — `resources/js/src/pages/<name>/`
   ```
   pages/<name>/
     index.tsx                 # list page (DataTableWithSidebar, breadcrumbs, bulk actions)
     components/
       <Name>Detail.tsx        # sidebar detail pane
       <Name>Form.tsx          # create/edit form
       <Name>Modal.tsx         # GenericModal wrapper around Form
   ```
4. **index.tsx pattern** (see `pages/user/index.tsx`):
   - React Query mutations via `<name>Api`
   - `useSidebarDetail` for detail sidebar
   - `useConfirmDialog` for deletes
   - `DataTableWithSidebar` + column configs
   - Modal open state + entity-to-edit state
   - Toast via `sonner`
5. **Modal** wraps Form in `GenericModal` (see `UserModal.tsx` / `RoleModal.tsx`)
6. **Router** — register lazy route in `resources/js/src/router/routes.tsx` with `permissions: [...]`
7. **Sidebar/nav** — update `resources/js/src/lib/sidebar.ts` (and i18n keys) when adding nav items

### C) Exceptions (existing, do not force full CRUD scaffold)
- **Auth** — `AuthController` + `routes/api/v1/auth.php` + `services/auth.ts` + `pages/login`, `pages/profile` (not index/Detail/Form/Modal CRUD)
- **Organizer auth** — `OrganizerAuthController` + `organizer-auth.php` (API only; no Web UI yet)
- **Organizer Admin Form** — status suspend/reactivate only (not full identity edit)
- **Organizer subscriptions** — Admin **oversight** only (`OrganizerSubscriptionController`): history list, assign, cancel — **not** full CRUD and not Web App self-serve
- **Events Admin Form** — **moderation** only (featured / capacity / status transition). **`monetized` is derived from paid ticket types** — cannot be forced contrary to tiers. Status changes **must** use `POST /events/{id}/transition` (PATCH status rejected).
- **Ticket types Admin** — oversight in Event Detail (list + disable/enable sales). Not top-level nav. Soft-delete OK; force-delete blocked if `quantity_sold > 0`. Full tier CRUD is Web App later.
- **Discount codes Admin** — read-only in Event Detail (+ ops create/validate APIs). Scope enforced in queries.
- **Participations Admin** — oversight nested in Event Detail (list, promote waitlist, cancel). Join API is admin stand-in; Web App owns participant join UX. Not a mandatory full CRUD scaffold page.
- **Event form fields Admin** — **read-only** schema oversight in Event Detail (`FormFieldOversight`). Organizers author fields on Web App (later). Ops store/remove APIs exist for tests; remove soft-handles answered fields (`active=false`).
- **Invitation templates Admin** — read-only `GET /events/{id}/invitation-template`; ops store/update. Web App owns designer UI.
- **QR Scan History Admin** — list page `/qr-scan-logs` (filter event/result) + Event Detail **Check-in dashboard** stats. Scanner UI is Web App; `POST /qr-scan-logs/validate` is admin/ops stand-in.
- **Payments / Payouts Admin (Phase 6 — full Admin System, not oversight-only):** `pages/payout/` workflow (request → approve/reject → record payment). Event Detail **Financial summary**. Settings → Commission rate. Charge endpoint for Web App later.
- **Event add-ons Admin (Prompt 10):** read-only Analytics + announcements/certificates/feedback/sponsors/speakers/sessions on Event Detail. Organizer authoring is Web App.
- **Share Event (spec 12.3 MUST):** **explicitly deferred to Web App pack** — front-end share-link generation only; not forgotten.
- **Organization** — profile/settings style (`getProfile` / logo uploads); page at `pages/organization/index.tsx` under Settings; service still extends `BaseApi`
- **Logs** — mostly read-only list + `LogDetail` (no Form/Modal create flow)
- **Settings mail** — form + test modal, not full BaseController CRUD entity
- **Trash** — reuses soft-delete endpoints; tabbed under `/trash` (users, roles, organizers, events)

