## High-Level Architecture
```
Browser → resources/views/app.blade.php → Vite React (resources/js/src)
       → axios /api/v1/* → routes/api.php → routes/api/v1/*.php
       → Api\*Controller (extends BaseController) → Model → DB
```
- Middleware: `EnsureJsonResponse` on API; Sanctum auth; Spatie permission aliases; **`admin.panel`** (`EnsureAdminPanelAccess`) on Admin Panel resource routes; **`organizer.web`** for organizer-auth me routes
- Traits on BaseController: `ApiResponseTrait`, `ApiFilterTrait`
- Domain services (non-controller): `MailService`, `LocationService`, `CommonServices`, **`EventStatusMachine`**, **`EventRegistrationGate`**, **`EventMonetization`**, **`ParticipationService`**, **`FormFieldValidationService`**, **`EventFormFieldService`**, **`QrTokenService`**, **`QrValidationService`**, **`EventQuota`**
- Domain ownership: **Users** (admin staff / participants) ≠ **Organizers** ≠ **Events** (belong to organizers). Packages gate how many events an organizer may create via `EventQuota`.

## Auth + User Types (Phase 1 — EventHub multi-tenant foundation)

EventHub participants are **Users** distinguished by `users.user_type` (`App\Enums\UserType`: `admin` | `user`). Organizers/Events are **not** in this phase.

| Concern | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| Column | `user_type` enum/string `admin\|user`. Original add was `2025_07_01_142344_...` (default was `user`). Phase 1 migration `2026_08_16_101700_set_users_user_type_default_to_admin` backfills **all existing rows to `admin`** and sets MySQL/pgsql default to `admin`. Do **not** edit already-run migrations. |
| Enum | `app/Enums/UserType.php` — `ADMIN='admin'`, `USER='user'` |
| Sanctum scopes | `app/Enums/SanctumAbility.php`: **`admin-panel`**, **`web-participant`** only. (Separate pre-existing session flag string `'locked'` is written onto token abilities by lock/unlock endpoints — not a login scope and not part of Phase 1.) |
| Admin login | `POST /api/v1/auth/admin/login` — **only** `user_type=admin`. Issues token ability `admin-panel`. Participant with correct password → **403** + `errors.error_code: participant_admin_login_forbidden` (distinct from 401 Invalid credentials). |
| Web login | `POST /api/v1/auth/login` — allowed for **both** `user` and `admin` (admins may later use Web App as participants). Issues `web-participant`. No Web App UI yet. |
| Token coexistence | Admin may hold **both** `admin-panel` and `web-participant` tokens. Login rotates **only** same-scope tokens (by ability + known token names). Logout deletes **current** token only. |
| Admin API guard | Middleware alias `admin.panel` requires authenticated `UserType::ADMIN` **and** token `can('admin-panel')`. Applied to `routes/api/v1/{users,roles,settings,logs,organizations}.php` and profile routes in `routes/api.php`. Auth login/logout/me/lock remain `auth:sanctum` only. |
| Public register | Sets `user_type=user` (participants). |
| Admin Users CRUD | Creates always force `user_type=admin`. **Updates ignore `user_type`** (read-only in Admin UI — no permission-gated write yet). |
| Admin UI | Users table: Type + Status columns; Type filter (All / Admin / Participant). Detail sidebar shows full useful fields including read-only type. |
| Tests | `tests/Feature/UserTypeAuthTest.php` — admin/participant login, 403 vs 401, dual tokens, web token blocked from `/users`, logout scope. |
| Seed | `RolePermissionSeeder` admin user remains `user_type=admin` (`admin@example.com` / `password`). |

## Organizers (Phase 2 — separate identity from Users)

Organizers are **not** Users. Own table, own Authenticatable model, own Sanctum tokens, own Web auth routes. Admins oversee records; they never “log in as” an organizer.

| Concern | Decision / behavior |
|--------|---------------------|
| Table | `organizers`: `business_name`, `contact_name`, `email` (**UNIQUE on this table only**), `phone`, `password`, `status` (`OrganizerStatus`: `active`\|`suspended`), timestamps, soft deletes |
| Email uniqueness | DB unique index on `organizers.email` only. **Allowed** to equal a `users.email` (unrelated identities). Validated with `unique:organizers,email` on register — never `unique:users`. |
| Auth guard | `config/auth.php` provider `organizers` + guard `organizer` (sanctum). Middleware alias `organizer.web` (`EnsureOrganizerWebAccess`). |
| Sanctum ability | `SanctumAbility::OrganizerWeb = organizer-web` (Web App organizer sessions). Never issued to Users; never grants Admin Panel. |
| Auth routes | `POST/GET /api/v1/organizer-auth/{register,login,logout,me}` — backend scaffolding only; **no login UI** (Web App later). |
| Suspension | Sets `status=suspended`, **revokes all organizer tokens immediately**. Login returns 403 `organizer_suspended`. **Does not delete or cascade events.** **Phase 4 must respect:** suspended organizer’s events stay visible to admins; organizer-web cannot mutate events while suspended (enforce via `organizer.web` + status check / policy). |
| Soft delete | Soft-delete keeps the row (`deleted_at`). Related future rows stay attached by `organizer_id`. **Future FKs (events, subscriptions): use `restrictOnDelete` (preferred)** so force-delete is refused while dependents exist; do **not** use Laravel’s default `cascade` on delete. Soft delete alone never hard-removes dependents. |
| Admin API | `OrganizerController` extends `BaseController`. Routes `routes/api/v1/organizers.php` + `admin.panel`. Permissions: `view organizers`, `suspend organizers`, `delete organizers`. Endpoints: list/show, suspend/reactivate, trash/restore/force/bulk. **No PATCH/POST create-update of identity fields** (405 if attempted). |
| Admin UI scope | View + status modal (suspend/reactivate) + soft-delete/trash. **Admins do not freely edit business name/contact/email/password** — Web App owns self-service. Flag product if later need “admin correction” edit. |
| FE | `pages/organizer/` (index+Detail+Form-status+Modal), `services/organizer.ts`, `types/organizer.ts`. Table **Package** = active subscription name; **Events** = `events_count`. Detail: subscription history + real event count. Trash `/trash/organizers`. Nav: `organizers`. |
| Activity log | `suspend` / `reactivate` / overridden `destroy` call `logActivity`; `restore` / `forceDestroy` / bulk via `BaseController`. |
| Tests | `tests/Feature/OrganizerModuleTest.php` |

## Packages & Subscriptions (Phase 3)

Access to event creation is gated by **subscription packages**. Admins fully CRUD packages; organizers will subscribe via Web App later. Admin can assign/cancel now for oversight.

### Data model (history, not a mutable column)

| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `packages` | Plan catalog: `name`, `description`, `price`, `event_quota` (**nullable**), `status` (`active`\|`archived`), timestamps |
| `organizer_subscriptions` | **One row per subscription period** (history). Columns: `organizer_id`, `package_id`, `status` (`active`\|`expired`\|`cancelled`), `started_at`, `expires_at` (**nullable**), timestamps. FKs: **`restrictOnDelete`**. |

**Do not** store “current package” as a column on `organizers`. Current plan = `Organizer::activeSubscription()`.

### Assumptions (explicit)

1. **`expires_at = null`** → not time-boxed until cancelled/replaced.
2. **`event_quota = null`** → unlimited; **`0`** → no events. Use `App\Support\EventQuota` only (never falsy checks).
3. Assign cancels prior active rows and inserts history.
4. Delete package blocked if any subscription history; archive blocked if active subscribers.
5. **`events_created`** in quota payloads = **real** `organizer.events()->count()` (Phase 4a wired).

### Admin surface
- Packages: Settings CRUD (`pages/settings/packages/`). Subscriptions: Organizer detail oversight.
- Create event API calls `EventQuota::canCreateEvent` before insert.

### Tests
- `tests/Feature/PackageSubscriptionTest.php`

## Events (Phase 4a — Admin oversight + backend)

Events belong to organizers. This phase: schema, state machine, registration gates, Admin list/moderate. **Organizer Web App create UI is out of scope.**

### Tables

| Table | Notes |
|-------|--------|
| `event_categories` | `name` unique; soft deletes; Admin full CRUD; seeded defaults (Conference, Workshop, Concert, Sports, Networking, Festival) |
| `events` | `organizer_id` (restrictOnDelete), `event_category_id` (nullOnDelete), title, description, city, address, latitude/longitude (nullable DB), banner_path, featured, monetized, **status**, capacity (nullable=unlimited), **registrations_count** (stand-in until registrations module), registration_deadline, starts_at, ends_at, soft deletes |
| `event_images` | Gallery rows: `event_id`, `path`, `sort_order`. Prefer table over JSON so images can be removed/reordered individually. Cascade delete with event. |

### Status state machine (`App\Services\EventStatusMachine`)

Enum order: `draft → published → registration_open → sold_out → registration_closed → ongoing → completed → cancelled`

**Transition table (from → allowed to):**

| From | Allowed targets |
|------|-----------------|
| `draft` | `published`, `cancelled` |
| `published` | `registration_open`, `draft`, `cancelled` |
| `registration_open` | `sold_out`, `registration_closed`, `ongoing`, `cancelled` |
| `sold_out` | `registration_closed`, `ongoing`, `cancelled` |
| `registration_closed` | `ongoing`, `cancelled` |
| `ongoing` | `completed`, `cancelled` |
| `completed` | _(none — terminal)_ |
| `cancelled` | _(none — terminal)_ |

- **cancelled** is reachable from every non-terminal state **except** `completed`.
- Invalid transitions → **400** with `errors.error_code: invalid_status_transition`.
- API: `POST /api/v1/events/{id}/transition` `{ "status": "..." }`. PATCH must not set status.

### Capacity → sold_out (decision)

**Real-time computed check** against `registrations_count` vs `capacity`, then **fires** a state transition when appropriate:

- `EventRegistrationGate::isCapacityReached()` — Gate A only (`null` unlimited, `0` always reached, else `registrations_count >= capacity`).
- `EventStatusMachine::syncSoldOutFromCapacity()` — if status is `registration_open` **and** capacity reached → transition to `sold_out`. Does **not** look at deadline.
- Triggered on admin update of capacity/count and via `POST /events/{id}/sync-capacity`.

`registrations_count` is a column updated by future registration flows; Admin can set it for ops/tests until then.

### Two independent registration gates (`App\Services\EventRegistrationGate`)

| Gate | Method | Behavior |
|------|--------|----------|
| **A Capacity** | `isCapacityReached($event)` | Independent of deadline. Drives sold_out sync. |
| **B Deadline** | `isRegistrationDeadlinePassed($event)` | Independent of capacity. Blocks when `registration_deadline` ≤ now even if seats remain and status is still `registration_open`. |

`evaluate()` / `canAcceptRegistration()` applies status check, then **Gate B**, then **Gate A** as separate branches (never one combined condition). Exposed on Event as `registration_gates` append + `GET /events/{id}/registration-gates`.

### Other edge decisions

- **Lat/lng**: optional at DB; app requires **pair** if either is set (`validateLatLongPair`). Address is independently optional.
- **Cancelled**: remains in admin lists; soft-delete allowed; **force-delete forbidden** for cancelled (history intact).
- **Gallery delete**: unlinks file under `public/` (Organization logo pattern) then deletes DB row (`EventImage::deleteFileFromDisk`).
- **Suspended organizers**: events stay admin-visible; organizer-web mutation still blocked by organizer.web + status (Phase 2). Event create still checks quota for the organizer.

### Admin surface

| Concern | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| Events | `EventController`, `routes/api/v1/events.php`, `pages/event/` (index+Detail+moderation Form/Modal), `services/event.ts`, `types/event.ts`. Permissions: `view/create/edit/delete events`. Trash `/trash/events`. |
| Categories | `EventCategoryController`, `event-categories.php`, Settings `pages/settings/event-categories/`, `services/eventCategory.ts`. Permissions: `view/create/edit/delete event categories`. |

### Tests
- `tests/Feature/EventModuleTest.php` — transition table, invalid transition 400, dual gates, lat/lng pair, quota block, cancelled force-delete block, gallery file unlink, category CRUD.

## Ticket Types & Discount Codes (Phase 4b)

Core monetization: multiple named tiers per event. Admin oversight only in this phase.

### Tables

| Table | Notes |
|-------|--------|
| `ticket_types` | `event_id` (restrictOnDelete), `name`, `price`, `quantity_limit` (null=unlimited), **`quantity_sold` (stored counter)**, `sort_order`, `sales_enabled`, soft deletes |
| `discount_codes` | `code`, `event_id` nullable, `organizer_id` nullable, `type` (`percent`\|`fixed`), `value`, `usage_limit`, `usage_count`, `expires_at`, `active`, soft deletes. Unique `(event_id, code)`. |

### quantity_sold — stored counter + Phase 6 atomic locking (REQUIRED)

**Decision: stored counter column**, not computed from participations (keeps claim O(1); refund/cancel use explicit atomic release so we do not double-count).

**Phase 6 Participation MUST claim inventory with an atomic conditional UPDATE** — never application read-then-write:

```sql
UPDATE ticket_types
SET quantity_sold = quantity_sold + :qty
WHERE id = :id
  AND deleted_at IS NULL
  AND sales_enabled = 1
  AND (quantity_limit IS NULL OR quantity_sold + :qty <= quantity_limit)
```

- Affected rows `= 1` → success; `= 0` → sold out / disabled / lost race.
- Helpers ready now: `TicketType::claimQuantityAtomically($id, $qty)` / `releaseQuantityAtomically($id, $qty)`.
- Wrap claim + participation insert in one DB transaction. On refund/cancel: atomic decrement with `WHERE quantity_sold >= :qty`; never double-release.
- Optional later: `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` in the same transaction for multi-line baskets.

### monetized consistency

`events.monetized` is **derived**: true iff any non-deleted ticket type has `price > 0`.
- `EventMonetization::syncMonetized()` after ticket-type create/delete.
- Admin PATCH cannot force `monetized` contrary to ticket types (400).

### Discount code scope (DB/query, not UI-only)

`DiscountCode::scopeUsableForEvent($event)`:
- Event-scoped (`event_id` set): only that event matches.
- Organizer-wide (`event_id` null + `organizer_id`): only that organizer’s events.
- `POST /events/{id}/discount-codes/validate` — event A’s code → 404 on event B.

### Admin surface

| Concern | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| Ticket types | Event Detail sidebar; `GET /events/{id}/ticket-types`; `POST /ticket-types/{id}/disable-sales` / `enable-sales`. Soft delete; force-delete blocked if sales. |
| Discount codes | Read-only on Event Detail; `GET /events/{id}/discount-codes`. |

### Tests
- `tests/Feature/TicketTypeModuleTest.php` — monetized sync, atomic claim, soft/force delete, discount scope.

## Participations (Phase 4c)

Links a **User** (participant) to an **Event**, optional **TicketType**, JSON `custom_field_answers` (validated at submit by **Phase 5a** `FormFieldValidationService`), nullable unique `qr_token` (**Phase 5b** invitation/QR).

### Status enum (final — Phase 6 + Phase 9 depend on this)

`ParticipationStatus`: **`waitlisted` | `joined` | `paid` | `checked_in` | `cancelled`**

| Status | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| waitlisted | Capacity/ticket full; awaiting promotion |
| joined | Confirmed seat (payment may still be pending) |
| paid | Payment confirmed — **synced from Payment SoT (Phase 6)** |
| checked_in | Attendee checked in (Phase 9) |
| cancelled | Withdrawn; **excluded from unique (user,event) index** |

Seat-occupying (count toward capacity / `registered_count`): `joined`, `paid`, `checked_in`.

### Payment status boundary (Phase 6 MUST follow)

- **Source of truth:** `payments` table (Phase 6) for money movement.
- **Mirror on participation:** `payment_status` enum `not_required | pending | paid | refunded | failed` — denormalized for admin UI/queries.
- Phase 6 syncs `participations.payment_status` (and may set `status=paid`) from Payment records. **Do not** invent a second ledger that contradicts `payments`.

### Unique participation constraint (DB-level)

One **non-cancelled** participation per `(user_id, event_id)`:

- **SQLite (tests):**  
  `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX participations_user_event_active_unique ON participations (user_id, event_id) WHERE status != 'cancelled'`
- **MySQL:** generated column `active_user_event_key` = `IF(status = 'cancelled', NULL, CONCAT(user_id, '-', event_id)) STORED` + `UNIQUE (active_user_event_key)`  
  (NULLs do not collide → multiple cancelled allowed)

Migration: `2026_08_16_160000_create_participations_table.php`.

### Atomic ticket claim + transaction boundary

`ParticipationService::join` / `promoteFromWaitlist` run inside **`DB::transaction`**:

1. `lockForUpdate` on event (and ticket type when needed)
2. **`TicketType::claimQuantityAtomically()`** (Phase 4b helper — not reinvented)
3. `Participation::create(...)`

If create fails, the transaction rolls back the claim UPDATE. Verified by `test_transaction_rolls_back_claim_when_insert_fails`. Waitlisted creates **do not** claim quantity until promotion.

### Waitlist

When event capacity is full (or ticket claim fails with allowWaitlist), status=`waitlisted`. Admin `POST /participations/{id}/promote` moves to `joined` and claims ticket atomically when a seat opens.

### Live counters on Event

Appends: `registered_count` (synced `registrations_count`), `waitlisted_count`, `seats_remaining` (null if unlimited capacity).

### Admin surface

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /events/{id}/participations` | Per-event oversight + capacity snapshot |
| `GET /participations` | Cross-event list (filter event_id / organizer_id) |
| `POST /participations` | Admin join stand-in |
| `POST /participations/{id}/promote` | Waitlist → joined |
| `POST /participations/{id}/cancel` | Cancel + release ticket if seat held |

FE: `ParticipationOversight` inside Event Detail sidebar.

### Tests
- `tests/Feature/ParticipationModuleTest.php` — unique index scope, txn claim+insert, rollback, waitlist, promote, quantity race simulation, admin API.

## Event Form Fields (Phase 5a — Dynamic Form Builder backend)

Organizers will design custom registration fields per event on the Web App. This phase stores the **schema** and validates `participations.custom_field_answers` at **submission time only**. Admin gets read-only visibility.

### Table `event_form_fields`

Migration: `2026_08_16_170000_create_event_form_fields_table.php`

| Column | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `event_id` | FK → events, `restrictOnDelete` |
| `key` | Slug-like field id |
| `label` | Display label |
| `type` | `FormFieldType`: `text` \| `number` \| `select` \| `checkbox` \| `date` |
| `options` | JSON (select / multi-checkbox choices); null for boolean checkbox / text / number / date |
| `required` | boolean |
| `sort_order` | unsigned int |
| `active` | Soft-handle flag — `false` = deactivated (kept for historical display) |

**Compound unique:** `$table->unique(['event_id', 'key']);` — key unique **within an event**, not globally.

### No FK from answers → schema (critical)

Answers are a JSON snapshot on `participations.custom_field_answers`. There is **no** foreign key tying answer keys to `event_form_fields`. Schema edits after join **must not** invalidate old rows. Validation runs only in `FormFieldValidationService` at join/submit.

### Soft-handle delete

`EventFormFieldService::remove()`:
- If any participation for that event has `custom_field_answers` containing the field `key` → set `active=false` (keep row).
- Else → hard-delete.

Inactive fields are **not** required by validation (only `active` schema applies to new submits).

### Validation service (standalone + wired)

`FormFieldValidationService::validate($event, $answers)` / `validateOrFail()`:
- Required active fields must be present (typed emptiness rules; boolean checkbox `false` counts as present).
- Type checks: text, number, date, select ∈ options, checkbox bool or multi-option list ∈ options.
- Extra keys in answers are allowed (forward/historical compatible).

`ParticipationService::join` calls `validateOrFail` **before** the DB transaction.

### Admin / API surface

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /events/{id}/form-fields` | Read-only schema (includes inactive unless `?active_only=1`) |
| `GET /event-form-fields` | Index (permission-gated) |
| `POST /event-form-fields` | Ops/test create (Web App will own authoring) |
| `DELETE /event-form-fields/{id}` | Soft-handle remove |

Permissions: `view event form fields`, `manage event form fields`.

FE: `FormFieldOversight` in Event Detail — **read-only** (no edit UI).

### Tests
- `tests/Unit/FormFieldValidationServiceTest.php` — standalone required/type/inactive/historical extras (14)
- `tests/Feature/EventFormFieldModuleTest.php` — compound unique, deactivate vs delete, join validation wire, admin list/store/destroy (8)

## Invitation + QR (Phase 5b)

Digital invitation templates + cryptographically random `participations.qr_token` + scan validation state machine + scan audit log. Scanner UI is Web App; Admin gets scan history + check-in stats.

### Tables

**`event_invitation_templates`** (`2026_08_16_180000_...`): `event_id` (unique), `config` JSON (flexible branding/layout), timestamps.

**`qr_scan_logs`** (`2026_08_16_180100_...`): `scanned_token`, nullable `participation_id` / `event_id`, `result` (`valid|already_used|invalid`), nullable `gate`, `scanner_user_id`, `scanner_organizer_id`, `meta` JSON. **Every attempt is logged** (success and failure).

**Token uniqueness (DB):** already on participations from Phase 4c:
`$table->string('qr_token')->nullable()->unique();` — generation retries on rare collision (`QrTokenService::assignToken`).

### When tokens are issued

`QrTokenService::ensureForConfirmed()` — cryptographically random `bin2hex(random_bytes(32))`, **not** sequential IDs or hashes of predictable fields.

Confirmed = `status=paid` OR free-and-joined (`joined` + `payment_status=not_required`) OR joined+payment paid. **Not** waitlisted / pending payment.

Wired from `ParticipationService::join` and `promoteFromWaitlist` after confirmed create/update. Phase 6 should call `ensureForConfirmed` when payment flips to paid.

### QR validation state machine (`QrValidationService`) — THREE distinct outcomes

Branch order (locked + transactional):

1. **invalid** — empty / token not found  
2. **invalid** — `status=cancelled` (BEFORE already_used)  
3. **invalid** — `payment_status=refunded` (BEFORE already_used)  
4. **already_used** — `status=checked_in` → log only, **no** check-in side effects  
5. **invalid** — not claimable (waitlisted, pending payment, etc.)  
6. **valid** — claimable → set `checked_in=true`, log; dispatch `ParticipationCheckedIn` (certificate listener — not inline)

Re-scan of a checked-in token → `already_used` + **separate** `qr_scan_logs` row; participation untouched.

### Check-in dashboard stats

`registered` (seat-occupying) / `arrived` (`checked_in`) / `absent` (= registered − arrived) + scan attempt counters.  
`GET /events/{id}/check-in-stats` · FE `CheckInStatsPanel` on Event Detail.

### Admin / API

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /qr-scan-logs` | History list (filter `event_id`, `result`) |
| `GET /qr-scan-logs/{id}` | Detail |
| `POST /qr-scan-logs/validate` | Ops/admin validate stand-in (`token`, optional `gate`) |
| `GET /events/{id}/qr-scan-logs` | Recent scans + stats |
| `GET /events/{id}/check-in-stats` | Dashboard numbers |
| `GET /events/{id}/invitation-template` | Read-only template |
| `POST/PATCH /event-invitation-templates` | Ops store/update |

Permissions: `view qr scan logs`, `manage qr scans`, `view invitation templates`, `manage invitation templates`.

FE: `pages/qr-scan-log/` (sidebar nav), `CheckInStatsPanel` in Event Detail.

### Tests
- `tests/Feature/QrInvitationModuleTest.php` — unique index, crypto token on free join, pending skips token, **valid / already_used / invalid**, cancelled→invalid (not already_used), refunded before already_used, re-scan dual logs, stats + API.

## Payments & Commission (Phase 6)

Financial core: WaafiPay charge → per-event payout requests → admin approve/record with snapshotted commission.

### Currency / WaafiPay
- Currency **USD** (`config/waafipay.php` / `WAAFI_CURRENCY`).
- Endpoint: `POST {WAAFI_BASE_URL}` (default `https://api.waafipay.net/asm`), `serviceName: API_PURCHASE`, `paymentMethod: MWALLET_ACCOUNT`.
- Credentials: `WAAFI_MERCHANT_UID`, `WAAFI_API_USER_ID`, `WAAFI_API_KEY` — never hardcoded, never logged, never sent to FE.
- **HTTP timeout: 180 seconds** (phone approval before response).
- Success ONLY when **both**: `responseCode === "2001"` AND `strtolower(params.state) === "approved"` (`WaafiPayService::isApprovedPayload`).
- Phone: `SomaliPhoneNormalizer` → `252XXXXXXXXX`.
- Errors: lookup table `WaafiPayService::ERROR_MAP` (not if/else chains).
- `reference_id` UNIQUE (`INV-{uuid}`); fresh UUID `requestId` per Waafi call.

### Pending cleanup
`ExpirePendingPayments` every 5 min. After `expires_at` (default **15 min**): payment→failed, participation→cancelled + payment_status failed, ticket quantity released.

### Payouts (per-event)
`payout_requests.commission_rate` snapshotted at **request create** from `CommissionSettings`. Display/approve/record use snapshot via `computeAmountsFromSnapshot()` — never live rate.

### Refund-after-payout (CLIENT REVIEW)
**Block** refund when `collected - amount < reserved/paid-out`. No automatic clawback — admin must handle outside this path.
API: HTTP 400 with human `message` **and** `errors.error_code: ["refund_blocked_payout_recorded"]` (same pattern as `participant_admin_login_forbidden` / `invalid_status_transition`). No admin refund UI yet — endpoint only.

### Double-payout
`PayoutService` request/approve/recordPayment: same `DB::transaction` + `lockForUpdate` on event and reducing payouts; re-validate outstanding inside txn.

### Admin FE
`/payouts`, Settings→Commission, Event Detail financial summary (`GET /events/{id}/finance`).

### Tests
`PaymentPayoutModuleTest` (13+) — Waafi both-conditions, mock HTTP, expire, snapshot, double-payout, refund block + `refund_blocked_payout_recorded` error_code, unique reference.

## Event Add-Ons (Prompt 10 — Spec §12)

Admin read-only oversight + backend models. Organizer authoring / participant submit UX = Web App.

### Share Event (12.3 MUST) — DEFERRED
**Explicitly deferred to the Web App pack** (front-end share-link generation only). Not implemented in Admin/backend. Do not treat as forgotten.

### Analytics (12.6 MUST)
`EventAnalyticsService::forEvent` — **efficient fixed query set (no N+1)**:
1. `events.views_count` column read
2. ONE `participations` `GROUP BY status` count query
3. ONE `payments` SUM (completed) via whereHas participation
4. ONE feedback AVG/COUNT query  
Also `event_views` log table + `POST /events/{id}/views` for Web App increments.  
FE: `EventAnalyticsPanel` on Event Detail.

### Certificates (12.5 HIGH)
- Table `certificates` with **`$table->unique('participation_id')`**
- `ParticipationCheckedIn` domain event dispatched from `QrValidationService` valid path only
- Listener `IssueAttendanceCertificate` → `CertificateIssuanceService::issueForParticipation` (exists check + lock + unique race catch) — **idempotent**
- Not inline in QR service

### Feedback (12.6 HIGH)
`EventFeedbackService::submit` requires `status === checked_in`. Unique per participation. Ops: `POST /event-feedback`. Tests cover joined/waitlisted rejection.

### Announcements / Sponsors / Speakers / Sessions
Read-only nested GETs under `/events/{id}/…`. Models: `EventAnnouncement`, `EventSponsor` (tier enum), `EventSpeaker`, `EventSession`. FE: `EventAddOnOversight`.

